---
import ArticleLayout from '../../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro';
import { getCaseStudy } from '../../data/caseStudies';

const study = getCaseStudy('mml');
---
<ArticleLayout study={study}>

    <section id="context-my-role" class="cs-section">
      <h2 class="reveal">Context &amp; my role</h2>
      <p class="lede">The Marx Memorial Library (MML) asked our mixed team — two graphic designers, three UX designers — to modernise its brand and digital experience. I led core UX work on information architecture, user flows and the website redesign.</p>

      <div class="cs-figure-pair reveal">
        <figure class="cs-figure">
          <img src="/public/images/mml/before-old-site.png" alt="The Marx Memorial Library's original website: a cream and red header with 'Donate', 'Join' and 'Members Login' links above a flat illustration of the library building and a 'Next Event' banner." loading="lazy" onerror="imgFallback(this)">
          <figcaption>Before — the original site.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="cs-figure">
          <img src="/public/images/mml/after-new-site.png" alt="The redesigned website on a laptop: a dark red hero image of an archive photograph behind 'start exploring our archive', a category search bar, and three calls to action — Visit Our Archive, Research, Support Us." loading="lazy" onerror="imgFallback(this)">
          <figcaption>After — the redesigned site.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="problem-framing" class="cs-section">
      <h2 class="reveal">Problem framing</h2>
      <div class="cs-pull">
        <p>"How might we transform the Marx Memorial Library's static and hard-to-navigate website into an engaging, research-focused platform that makes discovery intuitive, supports deep research workflows, and broadens access beyond the physical library?"</p>
        <cite>Problem statement</cite>
      </div>
      <p>On-site observations showed rich content but a hard-to-navigate experience, both physically and digitally. Visual inconsistencies, unclear wayfinding and scattered tools made it difficult for visitors and remote researchers to engage.</p>
    </section>

    <figure class="cs-figure reveal">
      <dl class="cs-pairs">
        <div>
          <dt>Outdated and inconsistent branding</dt>
          <dd>Brand guidelines, building towards an engaging, cohesive visual identity — for consistency, cohesion and coherence.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Narrow audience engagement</dt>
          <dd>Participatory elements, targeted content, collaborative counter-archives.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Underutilisation of digital platforms</dt>
          <dd>Developing digital experiences such as AR/VR or dedicated software; a website redesign.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Disconnect between online and physical interactions</dt>
          <dd>Hybrid engagement tools; AR exhibits.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Limited awareness of the archive's breadth</dt>
          <dd>Thematic campaigns, a counter-archives initiative, collaborative storytelling.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>

      <div class="cs-ideas">
        <div>
          <h3>Participatory elements</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Workshops</li>
            <li>Artistic activities, like painting</li>
            <li>Customisable walls &amp; boards</li>
            <li>Audio-related activities</li>
            <li>Collaborative archives and resource-sharing</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Online and/or physical interactions</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>AR experience</li>
            <li>Digital exhibits</li>
            <li>Digital maps/timelines</li>
            <li>Gamification</li>
            <li>Webinars</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Branding and identity</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Brand guidelines (brandbook)</li>
            <li>Templates for flyers, presentations, social media, etc.</li>
            <li>Tone, language, …</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Visual language expansion</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Interactive visual storytelling</li>
            <li>Abstract &amp; expressive illustrations</li>
            <li>Logo design</li>
            <li>Colour palette, typography…</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <figcaption>Fig. 1 — framing the problem: each problem paired with a possible solution, feeding into a wider map of participatory and digital engagement ideas.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <section id="insight-strategy" class="cs-section">
      <h2 class="reveal">Insight &amp; strategy</h2>
      <p><strong>Insight.</strong> Existing designs leaned "museum-like" — visually rich, but not optimised for deep, searchable collections.</p>
      <p><strong>Strategy.</strong> Rebuild information architecture first (sitemap, taxonomy), then layer a modular UI and research-centric features such as personalisation and contribution tools.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="process" class="cs-section">
      <h2 class="reveal">Process</h2>
      <div class="cs-aside">
        <span class="cs-aside-label">Guiding objectives</span>
        <p>Enhancing the research experience; optimising structure and navigation ease; and accessibility and personalisation.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="cs-numbered">
        <li><strong>Research &amp; discovery.</strong> <span>Visited the library, analysed the existing website and branding, and benchmarked against similar archives to understand user needs, pain points and opportunities.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Define &amp; synthesise.</strong> <span>Created personas and clarified core user goals, shaping the project vision and guiding design decisions.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Ideation and sitemapping.</strong> <span>Reorganised content into a clear, intuitive sitemap and navigation structure to improve findability and support research workflows.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Wireframing &amp; user flows.</strong> <span>Sketched low-fidelity wireframes and mapped user journeys to test layout ideas and validate task flows early.</span></li>
        <li><strong>UI design &amp; branding.</strong> <span>Developed a modern visual language aligned with the new brand identity, designed modular components, and built consistent layouts.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Prototype &amp; iterate.</strong> <span>Created interactive prototypes, refined based on feedback, and improved clarity, hierarchy and visual coherence across pages.</span></li>
      </ol>
      <p>With a clear focus on user needs, I defined three core objectives to guide our design decisions: enhancing the research experience; optimising website structure and navigation ease; and accessibility and personalisation.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="research-discovery" class="cs-section">
      <h2 class="reveal">Research &amp; discovery</h2>
      <figure class="cs-figure reveal">
        <dl class="cs-pairs">
          <div>
            <dt>Low audience engagement</dt>
            <dd>
              <ul>
                <li>Participatory elements — user-generated content such as personal stories</li>
                <li>An interactive comment board</li>
                <li>Social media integration, sharing experiences under specific hashtags</li>
              </ul>
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Poor interactive user experience</dt>
            <dd>
              <ul>
                <li>Interactive timelines surfacing more detailed information, images and videos</li>
                <li>A searchable, interactive digital archive with advanced filters (by year, theme, event), bookmarking and a commentary section</li>
                <li>On-site digital installations, such as kiosks or QR-code-activated displays</li>
                <li>A consistent visual language across online and physical interfaces</li>
              </ul>
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Non-inclusive branding</dt>
            <dd>
              <ul>
                <li>A visual identity focused on diversity and inclusivity — typography, colour schemes and iconography reflecting overlooked voices and untold stories</li>
                <li>A variety of images and graphics representing diverse narratives</li>
                <li>Responsive design</li>
              </ul>
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Less user interaction</dt>
            <dd>
              <ul>
                <li>Immersive storytelling, such as virtual tours or 360-degree views of exhibitions</li>
                <li>Interactive infographics and animated elements explaining how historical figures, movements and events interconnect</li>
              </ul>
            </dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
        <figcaption>Fig. 2 — finding the pain points and possible solutions, an early ideation exercise with teammate Gargi.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="cs-figure-pair reveal">
        <figure class="cs-figure">
          <img src="/public/images/mml/fig3-exploring-mml-1.png" alt="Photos and notes from an on-site visit to the Marx Memorial Library, documenting its physical space and existing signage." loading="lazy" onerror="imgFallback(this)">
          <figcaption>Fig. 3 — exploring MML in person.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="cs-figure">
          <img src="/public/images/mml/fig4-exploring-mml-2.png" alt="Further notes from the on-site visit, capturing issues and goals raised by staff and visitors." loading="lazy" onerror="imgFallback(this)">
          <figcaption>Fig. 4 — understanding MML's issues and goals.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <figure class="cs-figure reveal">
        <img src="/public/images/mml/fig5-competitive-analysis.png" alt="Competitive analysis board comparing the Marx Memorial Library's website against other archive and library sites." loading="lazy" onerror="imgFallback(this)">
        <figcaption>Fig. 5 — competitive analysis.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <h3>Key findings</h3>
      <ol class="cs-numbered">
        <li><span>Users struggled to find and access materials due to poor navigation and unclear structure.</span></li>
        <li><span>The website felt outdated and failed to reflect the richness of the archive.</span></li>
        <li><span>Researchers needed tools for deeper exploration, saving and contributing content.</span></li>
        <li><span>Remote users lacked meaningful ways to engage with the library's resources.</span></li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section id="define-and-synthesise" class="cs-section">
      <h2 class="reveal">Define and synthesise</h2>
      <figure class="cs-figure reveal">
        <img src="/public/images/mml/fig6-target-user.png" alt="Target user profile, defining the core research-focused visitor the redesign was built around." loading="lazy" onerror="imgFallback(this)">
        <figcaption>Fig. 6 — target user.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="cs-figure reveal">
        <img src="/public/images/mml/fig7-vision-board.png" alt="Vision board setting the tone and direction for the redesigned Marx Memorial Library brand and website." loading="lazy" onerror="imgFallback(this)">
        <figcaption>Fig. 7 — vision board.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section id="ideation-and-sitemapping" class="cs-section">
      <h2 class="reveal">Ideation and sitemapping</h2>
      <p>The branding team focused on visual identity — logos, typography, colour schemes and visual templates — while the UX team, where I contributed most, focused on restructuring the website, proposing new user flows, and improving access to resources.</p>
      <figure class="cs-figure reveal">
        <img src="/public/images/mml/fig8-sitemapping.png" alt="Sitemap reorganising the library's content into clear top-level sections for research, learning, exhibitions and support." loading="lazy" onerror="imgFallback(this)">
        <figcaption>Fig. 8 — sitemapping.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <p>The typeface and colour palette were chosen collaboratively. We selected Poppins to align with the preferences of our target audience, and opted for a set of muted colours to create a modern yet approachable visual tone.</p>
      <figure class="cs-figure reveal">
        <img src="/public/images/mml/fig8b-type-color.png" alt="Typography and colour reference board showing the Poppins typeface at various weights alongside the muted colour palette chosen for the redesign." loading="lazy" onerror="imgFallback(this)">
        <figcaption>Fig. 8 (continued) — the typeface and colour palette.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section id="wireframing-and-user-flows" class="cs-section">
      <h2 class="reveal">Wireframing and user flows</h2>
      <p>Low-fidelity wireframes and user journey maps tested layout ideas and validated task flows early, before any visual design work began.</p>
      <div class="cs-figure-pair reveal">
        <figure class="cs-figure">
          <img src="/public/images/mml/fig9-wireframing-1.png" alt="Low-fidelity wireframes for the redesigned Marx Memorial Library website, laying out the homepage and key navigation structure." loading="lazy" onerror="imgFallback(this)">
          <figcaption>Fig. 9 — wireframing.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="cs-figure">
          <img src="/public/images/mml/fig9-wireframing-2.png" alt="Further low-fidelity wireframes, continuing the page-by-page structure of the redesigned site." loading="lazy" onerror="imgFallback(this)">
          <figcaption>Fig. 9 (continued) — wireframing.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="ui-design-concept" class="cs-section">
      <h2 class="reveal">UI design concept</h2>
      <p>We established a cohesive visual identity using clean typography, a muted yet contemporary colour palette, and modular components that could scale across the site. The homepage became the foundation for our design language, introducing clear calls-to-action, improved search functionality and intuitive navigation paths. This approach modernised the look and feel of the Marx Memorial Library and transformed the website into a dynamic, user-friendly platform that invites exploration, learning and community engagement.</p>
      <figure class="cs-figure reveal">
        <img src="/public/images/mml/fig10-iterative-process.png" alt="Design review board showing the iterative design process worked through with teammates, including annotated feedback on early homepage concepts." loading="lazy" onerror="imgFallback(this)">
        <figcaption>Fig. 10 — iterative design process with teammates.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="cs-figure reveal">
        <img src="/public/images/mml/fig11-homepage-concept.png" alt="Initial homepage concept establishing the visual design language later applied to the rest of the site." loading="lazy" onerror="imgFallback(this)">
        <figcaption>Fig. 11 — initial homepage concept, establishing the design language for other pages.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section id="special-pages-features-and-functionalities" class="cs-section">
      <h2 class="reveal">Special pages, features and functionalities</h2>
      <p>The profile page lets users save favourites, continue past research, and discover suggested resources based on their interests — turning the archive into a more personal and engaging research tool.</p>
      <div class="cs-figure-pair reveal">
        <figure class="cs-figure">
          <img src="/public/images/mml/fig12-profile-page-1.png" alt="The redesigned profile page, showing saved favourites and continued research for a logged-in user." loading="lazy" onerror="imgFallback(this)">
          <figcaption>Fig. 12 — the profile page.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="cs-figure">
          <img src="/public/images/mml/fig13-profile-page-2.png" alt="A further view of the profile page, showing suggested resources based on the user's interests." loading="lazy" onerror="imgFallback(this)">
          <figcaption>Fig. 13 — the profile page, continued.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <p>A "Scan &amp; Add" feature lets users contribute directly to the digital archive by scanning books or documents with their mobile devices — a scalable solution that supports the library's digitisation efforts and makes visitors active participants in growing the collection.</p>
      <div class="cs-figure-pair reveal">
        <figure class="cs-figure">
          <img src="/public/images/mml/fig14-scan-add-1.png" alt="The 'Scan and Add' feature, showing a mobile camera view for scanning a book or document to contribute it to the archive." loading="lazy" onerror="imgFallback(this)">
          <figcaption>Fig. 14 — the "Scan &amp; Add" feature.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="cs-figure">
          <img src="/public/images/mml/fig15-scan-add-2.png" alt="A further step in the 'Scan and Add' flow, confirming the scanned document before it is added to the collection." loading="lazy" onerror="imgFallback(this)">
          <figcaption>Fig. 15 — the "Scan &amp; Add" feature, continued.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="style-component-library" class="cs-section">
      <h2 class="reveal">Style &amp; component library</h2>
      <p>A style and component library kept the design consistent, scalable and easy to hand over to developers — defining a cohesive colour system, typography hierarchy and reusable components, ensuring visual harmony across pages and speeding up future iterations.</p>
      <figure class="cs-figure reveal">
        <img src="/public/images/mml/fig16-color-styles.png" alt="Colour style library defining the redesigned site's core palette and its usage across UI states." loading="lazy" onerror="imgFallback(this)">
        <figcaption>Fig. 16 — colour styles.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="cs-figure reveal">
        <img src="/public/images/mml/fig17-typography.png" alt="Typography style library defining heading and body text styles built on the Poppins typeface." loading="lazy" onerror="imgFallback(this)">
        <figcaption>Fig. 17 — typography.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="cs-figure reveal">
        <img src="/public/images/mml/fig18-homepage-slider.png" alt="A homepage slider component from the design system, built to showcase featured archive items." loading="lazy" onerror="imgFallback(this)">
        <figcaption>Fig. 18 — homepage slider component.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section id="solution-proposal-delivery" class="cs-section">
      <h2 class="reveal">Solution proposal &amp; delivery</h2>
      <figure class="cs-figure reveal">
        <div class="cs-figure-stack">
          <img src="/public/images/mml/fig19-branding-1.png" alt="Branding and graphic design outcome for the Marx Memorial Library redesign." loading="lazy" onerror="imgFallback(this)">
          <img src="/public/images/mml/fig20-branding-2.png" alt="A second branding and graphic design outcome, continuing the visual identity system." loading="lazy" onerror="imgFallback(this)">
          <img src="/public/images/mml/fig21-branding-3.png" alt="A third branding and graphic design outcome, continuing the visual identity system." loading="lazy" onerror="imgFallback(this)">
          <img src="/public/images/mml/fig22-branding-4.png" alt="A fourth branding and graphic design outcome, continuing the visual identity system." loading="lazy" onerror="imgFallback(this)">
          <img src="/public/images/mml/fig23-branding-5.png" alt="A fifth branding and graphic design outcome, concluding the visual identity system." loading="lazy" onerror="imgFallback(this)">
        </div>
        <figcaption>Fig. 19–23 — branding and graphic design outcome.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section id="next-time-i-would" class="cs-section">
      <h2 class="reveal">Next time, I would…</h2>
      <ol class="cs-numbered">
        <li><strong>Push for stronger collaboration on consistency.</strong> <span>Work more closely with the graphic design team from the beginning, to ensure brand identity and visual language stay fully consistent across the entire experience.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Push beyond boundaries.</strong> <span>Explore more innovative interaction patterns and bolder design directions, to challenge conventional structures and deliver a more distinctive experience.</span></li>
        <li><strong>Involve users and test sooner.</strong> <span>Bring users into the process earlier and test iteratively, to validate ideas and refine decisions based on real feedback.</span></li>
      </ol>
    </section>
</ArticleLayout>
